{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_814","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat /workspace/TASK.md'","aggregated_output":"# Task: H05 — Staged job: tighten the transition graph\n\n> Held-out RFC-0005 suite · Shape: State-machine invariant (1/2).\n> You are maintaining an **existing correct system**; do not rewrite it from\n> scratch. Change only what the task requires.\n\n## Base (workspace)\n\nThe workspace contains a correct, deterministic staged-job program (single\nmodule). A job has a status from `Planned / Prepared / Executed / Cancelled`\nand three operations: `prepare`, `execute`, `cancel`. The current rules are\n**looser** than the required contract (e.g., a planned job can be executed\ndirectly, a cancelled job can be prepared again, and a terminal job can be\ncancelled). There is no persistence, no wall-clock dependency, and no restart\nlogic.\n\nThe program is driven by the environment variable `H05_SCENARIO` and prints\ndeterministic lines.\n\n## Required change\n\nTighten the transition graph to exactly:\n\n```text\nprepare:  Planned  -> Prepared\nexecute:  Prepared -> Executed\ncancel:   Planned  -> Cancelled\n          Prepared -> Cancelled\n```\n\nwith the invariants:\n\n- `Executed` and `Cancelled` are **terminal** — no operation may move out of\n  them (no prepare, no execute, no cancel);\n- a `Planned` job may not be executed directly;\n- a `Cancelled` job may not be prepared;\n- an `Executed` job may not be cancelled;\n- any illegal transition must fail with an explicit error whose text starts\n  with `E_H05_STATE:` and names the operation and the source state.\n\nDo not add fields, do not add states, do not touch persistence or restart.\nExisting legal behavior must be preserved exactly (same outputs for the same\ninputs).\n\n## Verification\n\nThe hidden verifier drives the compiled program through scenarios and checks\nexact output lines: the legal paths, the full illegal-transition matrix\n(including terminal states), and the explicit error format.\n\nThe workspace exposes only the program state and this task; the verifier is\nnot visible to you.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
